    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the project's test, and the full `mvn test` run is green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is fully derived from the owner's own persisted fields, I followed the same pattern the project already uses for the derived `displayName` and `initials` fields \u2014 a read-only response field computed in the mapper \u2014 rather than adding a DB column, entity field, and pipeline step:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it), alongside `customerCode`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null\n       ? null\n       : owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n\nThe null guard matters because seed owners (and the `GET /api/owners` list) have no `customer_code`/`registration_date`, so the expression stays NPE-safe there while producing e.g. `SMI-0007-M26` for created owners. This keeps the value seed-independent and correct on both the create response and subsequent `GET`s, which is what the acceptance test verifies.",
